# Scripts carry a shebang (`#!/usr/bin/env bash` in install.sh, `#!/bin/sh` in the shim), which the
# kernel reads literally: stored with CRLF, the interpreter becomes `bash\r` and macOS and Linux
# refuse to start them (`env: bash\r: No such file or directory`). Normalising on the way into the
# repository keeps that from coming back from a Windows checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
